{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Amiodarone\", \"id\": \"D000638\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bradycardia\", \"id\": \"D001919\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"hypothermia\", \"id\": \"D007035\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"respiratory failure\", \"id\": \"D012131\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"amiodarone\", \"id\": \"D000638\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"atrial fibrillation\", \"id\": \"D001281\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"thyroxine\", \"id\": \"D013974\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"steroids\", \"id\": \"D013256\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"levothyroxine\", \"id\": \"D013974\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"levothyroxine\", \"id\": \"D013974\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"iodine\", \"id\": \"D007455\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"amiodarone\", \"id\": \"D000638\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"amiodarone\", \"id\": \"D000638\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"thyroid disease\", \"id\": \"D013959\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"Amiodarone","id":"D000638","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"bradycardia","id":"D001919","label":"Disease"},{"text":"hypothermia","id":"D007035","label":"Disease"},{"text":"respiratory failure","id":"D012131","label":"Disease"},{"text":"atrial fibrillation","id":"D001281","label":"Disease"},{"text":"levothyroxine","id":"D013974","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"steroids","id":"D013256","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"iodine","id":"D007455","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"thyroid disease","id":"D013959","label":"Disease"}],"head":"iodine","head_id":"D007455","pairs":[{"head":"Amiodarone","tail":"bradycardia","head_id":"D000638","tail_id":"D001919"},{"head":"Amiodarone","tail":"hypothermia","head_id":"D000638","tail_id":"D007035"},{"head":"Amiodarone","tail":"respiratory failure","head_id":"D000638","tail_id":"D012131"},{"head":"Amiodarone","tail":"atrial fibrillation","head_id":"D000638","tail_id":"D001281"},{"head":"Amiodarone","tail":"thyroid disease","head_id":"D000638","tail_id":"D013959"},{"head":"levothyroxine","tail":"bradycardia","head_id":"D013974","tail_id":"D001919"},{"head":"levothyroxine","tail":"hypothermia","head_id":"D013974","tail_id":"D007035"},{"head":"levothyroxine","tail":"respiratory failure","head_id":"D013974","tail_id":"D012131"},{"head":"levothyroxine","tail":"atrial fibrillation","head_id":"D013974","tail_id":"D001281"},{"head":"levothyroxine","tail":"thyroid disease","head_id":"D013974","tail_id":"D013959"},{"head":"steroids","tail":"bradycardia","head_id":"D013256","tail_id":"D001919"},{"head":"steroids","tail":"hypothermia","head_id":"D013256","tail_id":"D007035"},{"head":"steroids","tail":"respiratory failure","head_id":"D013256","tail_id":"D012131"},{"head":"steroids","tail":"atrial fibrillation","head_id":"D013256","tail_id":"D001281"},{"head":"steroids","tail":"thyroid disease","head_id":"D013256","tail_id":"D013959"},{"head":"iodine","tail":"bradycardia","head_id":"D007455","tail_id":"D001919"},{"head":"iodine","tail":"hypothermia","head_id":"D007455","tail_id":"D007035"},{"head":"iodine","tail":"respiratory failure","head_id":"D007455","tail_id":"D012131"},{"head":"iodine","tail":"atrial fibrillation","head_id":"D007455","tail_id":"D001281"},{"head":"iodine","tail":"thyroid disease","head_id":"D007455","tail_id":"D013959"}],"relations":["D000638 | D001919","D000638 | D007035","D000638 | D012131","D000638 | D013959","D007455 | D013959"],"result":"$","tail":"thyroid disease","tail_id":"D013959","text":"Amiodarone-induced myxoedema coma. A 62-year-old man was found to have bradycardia, hypothermia and respiratory failure 3 weeks after initiation of amiodarone therapy for atrial fibrillation. Thyroid-stimulating hormone was found to be 168 uIU/mL (nl. 0.3-5 uIU/mL) and free thyroxine (FT4) was <0.2 ng/dL (nl. 0.8-1.8 ng/dL). He received intravenous fluids, vasopressor therapy and stress dose steroids; he was intubated and admitted to the intensive care unit. He received 500 ug of intravenous levothyroxine in the first 18 h of therapy, and 150 ug intravenous daily thereafter. Haemodynamic improvement, along with complete recovery of mental status, occurred after 48 h. Twelve hours after the initiation of therapy, FT4 was 0.96 ng/dL. The patient was maintained on levothyroxine 175 (g POorally daily. A thyroid ultrasound showed diffuse heterogeneity. The 24 hour excretion of iodine was 3657 (mcg (25-756 ( mcg). The only two cases of amiodarone-induced myxoedema coma in the literature report patient death despite supportive therapy and thyroid hormone replacement. This case represents the most thoroughly investigated case of amiodarone-induced myxoedema coma with a history significant for subclinical thyroid disease.","metrics":{"precision":0.6,"recall":0.6,"f1":0.6,"rel_tp":3,"rel_fp":2,"rel_fn":2}}